<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Bruce Lee returns for a periodic preventive visit a week after the back flare. The pain settled to 2 out of 10 within five days; he finished naproxen yesterday and is back to light training. He completed the health risk assessment beforehand. He has had no further seizures, sleeps about seven hours on most nights and eats regular meals between recording sessions. He has used no cannabis and drinks alcohol rarely. He has not driven since the seizure; a driver from the studio takes him to work. He asked which routine tests and vaccines are due at his age, and whether the seizure changes them. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic preventive medicine visit, age 18 to 39</td></tr><tr><td>Interval events</td><td>Back flare settled; no seizures</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Acetaminophen as needed; naproxen course completed</td></tr><tr><td>Substances</td><td>No cannabis since the seizure; alcohol rarely; never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours on most nights</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Trains daily: running, weights, flexibility and martial arts</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Lean; lost weight during the film schedule; now eats three meals a day with protein shakes</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours on most nights, down from four during the dubbing schedule</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco, alcohol and drugs</td><td>Never smoked; alcohol rarely; no cannabis since the seizure; no other drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Work pressure is high; supportive household; no low mood</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Not driving; wears a seat belt; no firearms at home; stunt work at heights paused</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>One long-term partner; no new partners</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

