    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic preventive visit completed</content>. Healthy 32-year-old man after a single seizure. Depression and alcohol screens are negative; drug use was asked about directly and discussed. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute back flare (M62.830)</content>. Resolved. [S]<list><item>Back to the core program; acetaminophen as needed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">First unprovoked seizure (R56.9)</content>. No recurrence in seven weeks; the seizure changes none of his routine screening, and no vaccine is withheld because of it. [S]<list><item>Two-month review in two weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>114/68 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Asked directly; occasional cannabis before the seizure, none since; counseling given at the first visit and reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; never tested; blood drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 18 to 79; blood drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once in adulthood with the triple panel (surface antigen, surface antibody and core antibody); he was raised in Hong Kong, where hepatitis B is common; blood drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 of 2 (HepB-CpG) today, without waiting for the screening result; dose 2 in one month</td></tr><tr><td>Tdap</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No booster recorded within ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Ages 27 to 45 by shared decision; with one long-term partner he chose not to have it</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and statin</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Statin screening applies from age 40; no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Prediabetes and diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended from 35 in adults with overweight or obesity; he is lean</td></tr><tr><td>Sexually transmitted infection screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>One long-term partner; no symptoms</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis vaccine (Tdap); Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Unhealthy Drug Use: Screening (2020); Screening and Testing for Hepatitis B Virus Infection: CDC Recommendations, United States, 2023 (2023); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B results at the two-month review. Hepatitis B vaccine dose 2 in one month. Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines in the autumn. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-13: two-month review: seizure-free, safety and driving, results of preventive tests, back pain and return to full training. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 15 minutes, with his consent. After the seizure he wanted to know what would happen if he were ever unable to speak for himself. He named a health care agent, a member of his household, recorded in the chart and not named here. He wants full treatment for any illness he could recover from, and wants the people treating him to explain things plainly to his agent. He asked that his health information be shared only with clinicians treating him and with his agent. He will revisit this yearly. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
